1
00:00:02,875 --> 00:00:04,208
[blade ringing]

2
00:00:08,041 --> 00:00:09,458
[metallic thwack]

3
00:00:11,625 --> 00:00:12,916
[sword slicing]

4
00:00:12,916 --> 00:00:14,916
[roaring reverberating]

5
00:00:16,166 --> 00:00:17,958
[roaring]

6
00:00:17,958 --> 00:00:19,708
[wind blasting]

7
00:00:19,708 --> 00:00:22,416
This is the closest to freedom

8
00:00:22,416 --> 00:00:24,375
I have been in a millennia.

9
00:00:24,375 --> 00:00:28,708
Yet three more chains
keep me imprisoned.

10
00:00:28,708 --> 00:00:29,916
Don't fear,

11
00:00:29,916 --> 00:00:32,375
the Forbidden Five hunt
the remaining blades

12
00:00:32,375 --> 00:00:33,875
as we speak.

13
00:00:35,333 --> 00:00:37,458
[roaring reverberating]

14
00:00:38,458 --> 00:00:39,958
[Roby] Yeah,
put that by the window,

15
00:00:39,958 --> 00:00:42,041
the backlight
will be Stang-Zoot-Cubed!

16
00:00:45,333 --> 00:00:46,666
That's the back of the piece.

17
00:00:46,666 --> 00:00:48,208
Turn it around, please.

18
00:00:51,416 --> 00:00:53,291
Huh. No, you were right,
it looked better before.

19
00:00:53,291 --> 00:00:54,291
[bot mumbling]

20
00:00:57,916 --> 00:00:59,291
When I'm done
with this remodel,

21
00:00:59,291 --> 00:01:01,125
this place
ain't gonna be a museum,

22
00:01:01,125 --> 00:01:03,000
it's gonna be a you-see-um,

23
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:04,166
with the huge crowds

24
00:01:04,166 --> 00:01:06,250
that are gonna
come through here!

25
00:01:08,041 --> 00:01:10,125
What, no reaction?

26
00:01:10,125 --> 00:01:12,958
Even Uncle Bleckt
used to at least give me a scowl

27
00:01:12,958 --> 00:01:14,958
for my genius wordplay.

28
00:01:16,041 --> 00:01:17,000
Hermes?

29
00:01:18,333 --> 00:01:20,083
-Hermes?
-[screeching awake]

30
00:01:21,583 --> 00:01:22,625
Hermes...

31
00:01:24,375 --> 00:01:26,541
I need you
to take this note to Geo

32
00:01:26,541 --> 00:01:28,083
in the Land of Lost Things.

33
00:01:28,083 --> 00:01:30,333
Another sculpture order.

34
00:01:30,333 --> 00:01:33,083
Tell him
we need more blue in here,

35
00:01:33,083 --> 00:01:34,208
but not azul.

36
00:01:34,208 --> 00:01:37,416
I'd say we're pretty full up
on azul.

37
00:01:37,416 --> 00:01:40,958
As they say,
too much Azul, is not a-cool.

38
00:01:40,958 --> 00:01:42,083
Hold a sec.

39
00:01:42,083 --> 00:01:43,416
Hey!
Wait, wait, wait, hey.

40
00:01:43,416 --> 00:01:44,583
That's gotta go

41
00:01:44,583 --> 00:01:46,083
right by the front entrance
to this floor.

42
00:01:46,083 --> 00:01:47,375
That statue of me

43
00:01:47,375 --> 00:01:49,583
is going to be the most
photographed art in here,

44
00:01:49,583 --> 00:01:52,541
so we have to place it
in prime selfie light.

45
00:01:56,458 --> 00:01:57,541
[smashing open]

46
00:01:58,791 --> 00:02:01,208
[stone crumbling]

47
00:02:01,208 --> 00:02:03,375
Hey, you can't just storm in--

48
00:02:04,708 --> 00:02:05,708
Wait...

49
00:02:05,708 --> 00:02:07,333
you're one of
the Forbidden Five!

50
00:02:07,333 --> 00:02:08,458
Ah!

51
00:02:08,458 --> 00:02:10,375
[blasting]

52
00:02:14,333 --> 00:02:15,625
[screeching]

53
00:02:17,291 --> 00:02:18,833
[screaming]

54
00:02:18,833 --> 00:02:19,708
[scream fading]

55
00:02:27,125 --> 00:02:29,291
What have they done to you?

56
00:02:34,625 --> 00:02:38,625
You think you can
sneak up on me, child?

57
00:02:38,625 --> 00:02:40,833
H'yah!
[smashing]

58
00:02:41,708 --> 00:02:43,458
Whatever you need
that blade for,

59
00:02:43,458 --> 00:02:45,666
Wyldfyre and the other Ninja
will kick your butt

60
00:02:45,666 --> 00:02:46,791
all over the Merged Lands

61
00:02:46,791 --> 00:02:47,791
before you can use it.

62
00:02:47,791 --> 00:02:50,666
[cackling wickedly]

63
00:02:50,666 --> 00:02:53,041
A funny one, you are.

64
00:02:53,041 --> 00:02:55,416
Let us see
how hilarious you find

65
00:02:55,416 --> 00:02:59,208
my Elemental Power of...
Decay...

66
00:02:59,208 --> 00:03:01,750
[screaming]

67
00:03:06,083 --> 00:03:09,458
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

68
00:03:09,458 --> 00:03:12,291
♪ Together we will rise ♪

69
00:03:12,291 --> 00:03:15,750
♪ We fight ♪

70
00:03:15,750 --> 00:03:18,833
♪ Be a ninja
for what's right ♪♪

71
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,208
You said you were taking me
to my parents.

72
00:03:28,208 --> 00:03:29,666
There's nothing up ahead.

73
00:03:29,666 --> 00:03:31,375
I mean, literally nothing.

74
00:03:31,375 --> 00:03:32,416
[snarling]

75
00:03:32,416 --> 00:03:33,500
Once again

76
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:35,458
you are misjudging
the situation.

77
00:03:35,458 --> 00:03:37,000
Oh, am I?

78
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:40,166
You see anything
but miles and miles of sand?

79
00:03:40,166 --> 00:03:41,208
Was I not right

80
00:03:41,208 --> 00:03:43,625
about Master Wu
causing the Merge?

81
00:03:43,625 --> 00:03:45,791
Just take me to my parents.

82
00:03:45,791 --> 00:03:46,833
Like you promised.

83
00:03:48,041 --> 00:03:50,041
That's what I'm doing.

84
00:03:50,041 --> 00:03:52,958
No, you're leading me
across an empty desert.

85
00:03:52,958 --> 00:03:54,250
I risked my life saving you.

86
00:03:54,250 --> 00:03:55,250
I believed--

87
00:03:55,250 --> 00:03:56,416
Stop.

88
00:03:58,916 --> 00:03:59,875
[gasping]

89
00:04:04,750 --> 00:04:07,625
[♪♪♪]

90
00:04:07,625 --> 00:04:08,625
[glint dinging]

91
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:11,250
How...

92
00:04:11,250 --> 00:04:14,083
how did you know this was here?

93
00:04:14,083 --> 00:04:17,458
I have many resources
hidden across the Merged Lands,

94
00:04:17,458 --> 00:04:19,916
as a contingency.

95
00:04:21,208 --> 00:04:25,000
Now perhaps
you will cease doubting me.

96
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,375
I...

97
00:04:27,375 --> 00:04:29,208
I'm sorry.

98
00:04:29,208 --> 00:04:31,791
Do you know how to pilot
such a vehicle?

99
00:04:31,791 --> 00:04:33,791
Yeah, pretty much.

100
00:04:33,791 --> 00:04:34,791
When I was a mech racer,

101
00:04:34,791 --> 00:04:36,041
my best friend Sor--

102
00:04:36,041 --> 00:04:37,791
Uh, a long time ago,

103
00:04:37,791 --> 00:04:40,125
someone taught me how to drive

104
00:04:40,125 --> 00:04:42,666
and pilot all kinds of vehicles.

105
00:04:42,666 --> 00:04:44,208
Hmm...

106
00:04:44,208 --> 00:04:45,791
Show me what you've learned.

107
00:04:50,708 --> 00:04:51,916
Huh...

108
00:04:51,916 --> 00:04:52,916
[inhaling thoughtfully]

109
00:04:52,916 --> 00:04:55,500
Okay, power should be...

110
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:57,250
[alarm ringing]

111
00:04:57,250 --> 00:04:58,333
[hits button, alarm shuts off]

112
00:04:58,333 --> 00:05:00,583
[wiper squeaking]

113
00:05:00,583 --> 00:05:03,083
[mariachi music playing]

114
00:05:03,083 --> 00:05:04,333
Yeah, that's there,

115
00:05:04,333 --> 00:05:05,416
so this is...

116
00:05:05,416 --> 00:05:07,958
[drone engine powers up]

117
00:05:10,583 --> 00:05:11,791
It has a drone?

118
00:05:11,791 --> 00:05:12,708
I-I mean, I knew that.

119
00:05:12,708 --> 00:05:13,875
Just confirming.

120
00:05:13,875 --> 00:05:14,875
There it is.

121
00:05:14,875 --> 00:05:15,958
Now to make it land...

122
00:05:18,583 --> 00:05:19,583
[pushing button]

123
00:05:23,041 --> 00:05:25,708
Got to make it land
on the jet...

124
00:05:27,458 --> 00:05:28,791
Ah!

125
00:05:28,791 --> 00:05:29,666
Fool!

126
00:05:33,958 --> 00:05:35,875
Whew!

127
00:05:35,875 --> 00:05:37,208
[engine powering up]

128
00:05:37,208 --> 00:05:40,083
I was going to hit that next.

129
00:05:40,083 --> 00:05:41,083
Buckle up!

130
00:05:44,833 --> 00:05:46,000
[power surges and backfires]

131
00:05:47,333 --> 00:05:48,750
Oh, right, uh...

132
00:05:48,750 --> 00:05:50,916
disengage landing gear.

133
00:05:50,916 --> 00:05:52,916
Uh, okay, now hold on to--

134
00:05:52,916 --> 00:05:53,958
[yelping] Whoa!

135
00:05:53,958 --> 00:05:57,041
[wailing]

136
00:05:59,416 --> 00:06:00,583
Hey, look!

137
00:06:01,541 --> 00:06:04,416
Maybe Ras travelled on this,

138
00:06:04,416 --> 00:06:06,166
and Arin dragged him?

139
00:06:06,166 --> 00:06:07,666
Oh, makes sense.

140
00:06:07,666 --> 00:06:10,041
Ras looked pretty hurt
last time we saw him,

141
00:06:10,041 --> 00:06:12,791
and it would explain
their strange tracks.

142
00:06:12,791 --> 00:06:14,250
What do you think, Frak?

143
00:06:14,250 --> 00:06:15,333
Love it. Super cool.

144
00:06:15,333 --> 00:06:17,750
You love Arin
pulling Ras on a sled?

145
00:06:17,750 --> 00:06:18,750
I'm sorry,

146
00:06:18,750 --> 00:06:20,458
I was kind of preoccupied

147
00:06:20,458 --> 00:06:24,166
wondering what that
terrifying-looking place is?

148
00:06:24,166 --> 00:06:25,875
I have no idea.

149
00:06:25,875 --> 00:06:28,833
Looks like the edge
of another realm that merged.

150
00:06:28,833 --> 00:06:30,791
We don't have to go there,
do we?

151
00:06:30,791 --> 00:06:32,541
It's probably full of puppets.

152
00:06:32,541 --> 00:06:33,416
I just know it.

153
00:06:33,416 --> 00:06:34,916
[sniffing]

154
00:06:34,916 --> 00:06:37,416
[grumbling]

155
00:06:37,416 --> 00:06:41,791
Yep, this sled
was definitely Ras's.

156
00:06:41,791 --> 00:06:42,958
[sniffing]

157
00:06:42,958 --> 00:06:44,750
[grumbling]

158
00:06:44,750 --> 00:06:46,541
Two sets of prints.

159
00:06:46,541 --> 00:06:48,250
If Ras was injured,

160
00:06:48,250 --> 00:06:49,916
it looks like he got better.

161
00:06:49,916 --> 00:06:51,083
Only two sets.

162
00:06:51,083 --> 00:06:53,375
Which makes it more likely
they are alone.

163
00:06:53,375 --> 00:06:55,125
No Forbidden Five.

164
00:06:55,125 --> 00:06:56,875
Where could the Five
have gone then?

165
00:06:56,875 --> 00:06:58,083
Who knows, who cares?

166
00:06:58,083 --> 00:06:59,541
We're back on track
to find Arin,

167
00:06:59,541 --> 00:07:01,416
and that's
all that matters, right?

168
00:07:01,416 --> 00:07:02,791
Let's go.

169
00:07:04,708 --> 00:07:07,708
[grumble barking]

170
00:07:07,708 --> 00:07:09,291
What is it, Riyu?

171
00:07:09,291 --> 00:07:11,458
[grumbling urgently]

172
00:07:12,708 --> 00:07:15,250
He wants us to follow him.

173
00:07:16,291 --> 00:07:18,083
Uh, that's
the opposite direction

174
00:07:18,083 --> 00:07:19,250
that Arin was headed!

175
00:07:19,250 --> 00:07:20,708
Maybe someone needs help.

176
00:07:20,708 --> 00:07:22,583
Riyu's never led us wrong.

177
00:07:22,583 --> 00:07:23,666
Well, he has led us

178
00:07:23,666 --> 00:07:25,458
to more than one noodle house
in the past.

179
00:07:25,458 --> 00:07:28,208
And was that wrong?

180
00:07:28,208 --> 00:07:29,500
Really?
We're just...?

181
00:07:29,500 --> 00:07:31,875
Um, okay, but for the record,

182
00:07:31,875 --> 00:07:33,666
I think this is a mistake.

183
00:07:33,666 --> 00:07:35,000
Noted.

184
00:07:36,416 --> 00:07:39,458
Hey there, Rapton here.

185
00:07:39,458 --> 00:07:42,750
Are you sick of the 9-5?

186
00:07:42,750 --> 00:07:44,125
[munching]

187
00:07:44,125 --> 00:07:48,625
Rapton is here to invite you
on the ride of a lifetime.

188
00:07:50,416 --> 00:07:53,958
We have a great
healthcare plan,

189
00:07:53,958 --> 00:07:56,333
and you'll be rich!

190
00:07:56,333 --> 00:07:59,083
And famous!

191
00:07:59,083 --> 00:08:01,875
No autographs, please.

192
00:08:01,875 --> 00:08:05,166
[♪♪♪]

193
00:08:05,166 --> 00:08:06,208
Join the Freebooters

194
00:08:06,208 --> 00:08:07,833
today!

195
00:08:09,416 --> 00:08:11,250
Hello, handsome.

196
00:08:14,500 --> 00:08:15,666
Whoa!

197
00:08:15,666 --> 00:08:16,666
[grumbling]

198
00:08:17,916 --> 00:08:19,833
What?

199
00:08:29,458 --> 00:08:31,291
Primary...

200
00:08:31,291 --> 00:08:33,166
electronics disrupted...

201
00:08:33,166 --> 00:08:34,083
secondary elements--

202
00:08:34,083 --> 00:08:36,416
Shh... Zane.

203
00:08:36,416 --> 00:08:38,125
Save your energy.

204
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,208
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

205
00:08:44,208 --> 00:08:46,916
What makes you think
you can just use our stuff?

206
00:08:46,916 --> 00:08:49,875
We stole all that gear
fair and square, lady!

207
00:08:50,916 --> 00:08:53,500
If it wasn't for
that Nindroid there,

208
00:08:53,500 --> 00:08:55,791
you and your poorly-named
"Freebooters"

209
00:08:55,791 --> 00:08:57,958
would all be smashed
against that cliff.

210
00:08:57,958 --> 00:09:00,291
Told you it was an awful name.

211
00:09:00,291 --> 00:09:01,458
The only reason

212
00:09:01,458 --> 00:09:04,208
you and your hair-piece
are still alive

213
00:09:04,208 --> 00:09:06,083
is because of Zane,

214
00:09:06,083 --> 00:09:08,916
who needs a lot of help
to survive this.

215
00:09:08,916 --> 00:09:12,875
So you are not only
going to let me use your gear,

216
00:09:12,875 --> 00:09:15,875
you are going to help me find
the pieces I need

217
00:09:15,875 --> 00:09:17,583
to save him.

218
00:09:17,583 --> 00:09:19,166
Have I made myself clear?

219
00:09:19,166 --> 00:09:20,375
[clearing throat]

220
00:09:20,375 --> 00:09:22,375
Uh, Freebooters,

221
00:09:22,375 --> 00:09:24,000
I, Rapton,

222
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:27,625
have decided
it's up to us to save Zane.

223
00:09:27,625 --> 00:09:30,250
So when Pixal here,
who's assisting me,

224
00:09:30,250 --> 00:09:31,500
asks for something,

225
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:32,416
let her have it.

226
00:09:32,416 --> 00:09:33,750
Unless it's like
super valuable,

227
00:09:33,750 --> 00:09:36,541
and then still ask--
ask me first.

228
00:09:36,541 --> 00:09:38,166
Also, this is definitely
my real hair.

229
00:09:39,416 --> 00:09:41,666
Get me more parts
like these, please.

230
00:09:43,666 --> 00:09:47,083
We are not going to lose
each other again, Zane.

231
00:09:47,083 --> 00:09:49,083
Whatever it takes.

232
00:09:52,666 --> 00:09:54,041
I don't get it.

233
00:09:54,041 --> 00:09:56,416
How did Jay play
this old game remotely?

234
00:09:56,416 --> 00:09:59,333
Nothing on the motherboard
allows remote access.

235
00:09:59,333 --> 00:10:00,500
Hmm...

236
00:10:00,500 --> 00:10:02,708
Did you check the fatherboard?

237
00:10:04,375 --> 00:10:06,625
I'm thinking
he cheated somehow.

238
00:10:06,625 --> 00:10:08,916
Only way he could have
beaten my high score.

239
00:10:08,916 --> 00:10:10,125
Check for cheat-ware.

240
00:10:10,125 --> 00:10:11,708
[sighing]

241
00:10:11,708 --> 00:10:14,500
If we could figure out
how he transmitted the signal,

242
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:17,208
we could trace it back
to Jay's location, and--

243
00:10:17,208 --> 00:10:19,083
--and force him to admit
he cheated!

244
00:10:20,291 --> 00:10:21,750
[groaning]

245
00:10:21,750 --> 00:10:23,875
[gasping] Yes!

246
00:10:23,875 --> 00:10:25,000
Ooh...

247
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:28,250
Somebody's getting another
"love scroll".

248
00:10:29,166 --> 00:10:31,250
Am not.
[giggling] Shut up.

249
00:10:31,250 --> 00:10:34,458
Okay, I totally am.
[guffawing]

250
00:10:34,458 --> 00:10:35,458
[gasping]

251
00:10:35,458 --> 00:10:36,458
No!

252
00:10:36,458 --> 00:10:38,625
What? Is Roby
breaking up with you?

253
00:10:38,625 --> 00:10:40,333
Let's go kick his little butt!

254
00:10:40,333 --> 00:10:42,083
No, Roby's hurt!

255
00:10:42,083 --> 00:10:44,166
The City of Temples
was attacked!

256
00:10:44,166 --> 00:10:45,458
[gasping]

257
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:47,583
Welcome to Arin Airlines,

258
00:10:47,583 --> 00:10:49,250
we've reached
cruising altitude, so--

259
00:10:49,250 --> 00:10:52,708
Your commentary
is not necessary.

260
00:10:52,708 --> 00:10:54,083
Hey, what's that?

261
00:10:56,291 --> 00:10:57,458
I know that place.

262
00:10:57,458 --> 00:10:59,083
Lloyd and I were there.

263
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:01,583
What are you doing?

264
00:11:01,583 --> 00:11:03,125
It looks like they need help.

265
00:11:03,125 --> 00:11:05,791
Stay focused
on the task at hand.

266
00:11:05,791 --> 00:11:07,291
We can't just ignore this.

267
00:11:07,291 --> 00:11:10,083
If you're distracted
by everything in your path,

268
00:11:10,083 --> 00:11:12,625
you'll never find your parents.

269
00:11:12,625 --> 00:11:15,375
That's why Lloyd
is so ineffectual,

270
00:11:15,375 --> 00:11:18,875
and he has clearly
passed his bad habits on to you.

271
00:11:18,875 --> 00:11:21,333
Time to prioritize

272
00:11:21,333 --> 00:11:23,375
your needs.

273
00:11:34,083 --> 00:11:35,333
Oh, wow!

274
00:11:35,333 --> 00:11:38,000
Look what we've found.

275
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:40,125
It's nothing.

276
00:11:40,125 --> 00:11:41,916
And over there, more nothing!

277
00:11:41,916 --> 00:11:43,500
When you get to know
Riyu better,

278
00:11:43,500 --> 00:11:45,125
you'll learn to trust him.

279
00:11:46,166 --> 00:11:48,583
If we'd stayed focused
on finding Arin,

280
00:11:48,583 --> 00:11:49,875
we might already have--

281
00:11:49,875 --> 00:11:51,416
[shrieking growl]

282
00:11:51,416 --> 00:11:53,083
Riyu, what gives?

283
00:11:53,083 --> 00:11:54,583
[grumbling]

284
00:12:01,041 --> 00:12:03,791
I'm... not hearing anything.

285
00:12:05,416 --> 00:12:06,791
Fan out!

286
00:12:06,791 --> 00:12:09,291
The blade must be nearby!

287
00:12:09,291 --> 00:12:12,083
We should have found it by now!

288
00:12:12,083 --> 00:12:14,541
[quietly] Now we know
where the Forbidden Five are.

289
00:12:14,541 --> 00:12:16,291
Well, one of them.

290
00:12:16,291 --> 00:12:17,791
That's Tyr.

291
00:12:17,791 --> 00:12:20,750
The leader
of the Dragonians we met.

292
00:12:20,750 --> 00:12:22,458
The ones that helped us
out of the river?

293
00:12:22,458 --> 00:12:25,500
What have the Forbidden Five
done to them?

294
00:12:25,500 --> 00:12:28,333
Is this what
you wanted to show us?

295
00:12:28,333 --> 00:12:29,750
[grumbling softly]

296
00:12:29,750 --> 00:12:31,541
[Lloyd] They look corrupted,

297
00:12:31,541 --> 00:12:34,000
maybe ancient magic.

298
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,375
The Five must've come through
the village after we did.

299
00:12:36,375 --> 00:12:38,291
Those poor Dragonians...

300
00:12:38,291 --> 00:12:42,041
[grumbling softly]

301
00:12:42,041 --> 00:12:43,000
[Tyr growling]

302
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:44,333
You fools.

303
00:12:44,333 --> 00:12:46,791
It's a small blade,
about this big,

304
00:12:46,791 --> 00:12:48,625
of a shimmering metal.

305
00:12:48,625 --> 00:12:51,333
ThunderFang said
you'd be able to sense it.

306
00:12:51,333 --> 00:12:53,875
What's wrong with you?

307
00:12:55,708 --> 00:12:57,875
He mean this?

308
00:12:59,458 --> 00:13:00,458
[snarling]

309
00:13:04,416 --> 00:13:05,666
[gasping]

310
00:13:05,666 --> 00:13:06,666
Ninja?

311
00:13:06,666 --> 00:13:08,541
[growling]

312
00:13:08,541 --> 00:13:11,208
Give that blade to me!

313
00:13:11,208 --> 00:13:14,041
Yeah, I'd say
this is what he's looking for!

314
00:13:14,041 --> 00:13:16,041
Ninja... go!

315
00:13:17,708 --> 00:13:19,833
Oh, dear.

316
00:13:19,833 --> 00:13:22,458
I do hope I'm following
these operating instructions

317
00:13:22,458 --> 00:13:24,916
from Master Zane correctly.

318
00:13:24,916 --> 00:13:26,083
"Just walk up to the portal

319
00:13:26,083 --> 00:13:29,166
and state
your desired destination."

320
00:13:29,166 --> 00:13:31,375
Take me to Roby!

321
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:36,708
No, state your destination.

322
00:13:36,708 --> 00:13:39,791
Take me to Roby town!

323
00:13:42,166 --> 00:13:43,958
[together]
The City of Temples!

324
00:13:47,041 --> 00:13:48,041
Let's go!

325
00:13:48,041 --> 00:13:50,416
Thanks, Mr. Frohicky.

326
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,916
Hey!

327
00:14:02,916 --> 00:14:04,791
When did that happen?

328
00:14:04,791 --> 00:14:06,750
That portal
wasn't active before.

329
00:14:06,750 --> 00:14:07,750
Who cares?

330
00:14:07,750 --> 00:14:09,333
My boyfriend's
way more important

331
00:14:09,333 --> 00:14:11,291
than stupid gates!

332
00:14:13,500 --> 00:14:15,041
[door smashing]

333
00:14:15,041 --> 00:14:17,083
Roby, what happened to you?

334
00:14:18,041 --> 00:14:20,333
[sighing] Wyldfyre...

335
00:14:20,333 --> 00:14:22,666
I knew you'd come.

336
00:14:22,666 --> 00:14:23,666
[weakly] Rawr.

337
00:14:23,666 --> 00:14:25,125
[gently] Rawr.

338
00:14:25,125 --> 00:14:26,458
Whoever did this to you,

339
00:14:26,458 --> 00:14:28,083
I'll heat blast them!

340
00:14:28,083 --> 00:14:29,375
Then resurrect them again,

341
00:14:29,375 --> 00:14:31,041
then heat blast 'em again!

342
00:14:31,041 --> 00:14:33,875
It was
one of the Forbidden Five.

343
00:14:33,875 --> 00:14:35,500
She got Hermes, too.

344
00:14:36,666 --> 00:14:38,833
[croaking weakly]

345
00:14:38,833 --> 00:14:41,208
The zootless jerk and her goons

346
00:14:41,208 --> 00:14:42,458
came for a weapon.

347
00:14:42,458 --> 00:14:45,541
The Five don't have
enough weapons already?

348
00:14:45,541 --> 00:14:47,666
I should know the importance

349
00:14:47,666 --> 00:14:50,541
of the Prismatic blade she took,

350
00:14:50,541 --> 00:14:52,333
but I don't.

351
00:14:52,333 --> 00:14:56,333
I used to think old lore
was a just waste of time,

352
00:14:56,333 --> 00:14:59,000
like the Source Dragons
being a myth,

353
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,125
but I was wrong.

354
00:15:01,125 --> 00:15:02,250
[groaning weakly]

355
00:15:02,250 --> 00:15:03,916
Let me help with that.

356
00:15:03,916 --> 00:15:06,083
Ah, thanks.

357
00:15:06,083 --> 00:15:08,000
My eyes are getting worse.

358
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:09,791
I can't read this,

359
00:15:09,791 --> 00:15:12,541
but the answers
could be in here,

360
00:15:12,541 --> 00:15:14,583
"The Sagas
of the Eternal Sources"

361
00:15:14,583 --> 00:15:17,166
by King Urd Leatherwing.

362
00:15:17,166 --> 00:15:19,666
It's a book of history
my family kept.

363
00:15:19,666 --> 00:15:21,458
You have to find out
what they're doing.

364
00:15:21,458 --> 00:15:24,416
You have to stop
the Forbidden Five.

365
00:15:24,416 --> 00:15:26,583
[coughing]

366
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:31,833
Shh...

367
00:15:31,833 --> 00:15:33,125
Roby.

368
00:15:33,125 --> 00:15:34,125
The Forbidden Five

369
00:15:34,125 --> 00:15:35,750
are going to be
the Forgotten Zero

370
00:15:35,750 --> 00:15:37,458
when I'm done with them.

371
00:15:37,458 --> 00:15:40,666
[coughing]

372
00:15:45,958 --> 00:15:47,208
[roaring]

373
00:15:48,625 --> 00:15:49,625
Come on!

374
00:15:49,625 --> 00:15:51,875
You were so nice before.

375
00:15:51,875 --> 00:15:53,000
Can't we all just be cool?

376
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:54,000
[snarling]

377
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:55,958
[rumbling]

378
00:15:55,958 --> 00:15:57,416
Quake works better

379
00:15:57,416 --> 00:15:59,000
against people who stay
on the grou--

380
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:00,375
[wailing]

381
00:16:00,375 --> 00:16:02,291
Tyr, buddy,
you got any tech on you?

382
00:16:02,291 --> 00:16:03,291
Anything at all?

383
00:16:03,291 --> 00:16:04,708
Guess not.

384
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,875
Then let's give Spinjitzu
another try.

385
00:16:11,875 --> 00:16:13,541
Did I do it?

386
00:16:13,541 --> 00:16:15,708
[wailing]
I don't think I did it!

387
00:16:15,708 --> 00:16:16,833
[grunting impact]

388
00:16:21,458 --> 00:16:23,708
[snarling]

389
00:16:23,708 --> 00:16:24,750
Whoa-ah!

390
00:16:24,750 --> 00:16:25,875
Unh!

391
00:16:28,791 --> 00:16:30,833
[stomping heavily]

392
00:16:30,833 --> 00:16:31,750
Uh-oh.

393
00:16:31,750 --> 00:16:33,208
I hate that sound.

394
00:16:40,041 --> 00:16:41,666
[grunting]

395
00:16:41,666 --> 00:16:42,666
[roaring]

396
00:16:42,666 --> 00:16:43,666
H'yah!

397
00:16:43,666 --> 00:16:44,708
Rah!

398
00:16:44,708 --> 00:16:46,875
That belongs to me.

399
00:16:46,875 --> 00:16:49,083
I don't know exactly
who it belongs to,

400
00:16:49,083 --> 00:16:51,708
possibly a giant,
creepy desert puppet,

401
00:16:51,708 --> 00:16:53,041
but I 100% know

402
00:16:53,041 --> 00:16:55,250
it doesn't belong
to the Forbidden Five!

403
00:16:55,250 --> 00:16:57,375
Everything we desire
belongs to us

404
00:16:57,375 --> 00:17:00,250
by right of conquest!

405
00:17:03,166 --> 00:17:04,208
H'yah!

406
00:17:20,791 --> 00:17:22,416
See, told you!

407
00:17:22,416 --> 00:17:23,375
Told me what?

408
00:17:23,375 --> 00:17:25,125
That we shouldn't follow Riyu.

409
00:17:25,125 --> 00:17:26,125
You noted it.

410
00:17:26,125 --> 00:17:28,083
Riyu can hear other dragons.

411
00:17:28,083 --> 00:17:31,041
I bet he could sense
the Dragonians were in trouble!

412
00:17:31,041 --> 00:17:32,208
Still shouldn't have followed!

413
00:17:32,208 --> 00:17:33,583
[deep roaring overhead]

414
00:17:33,583 --> 00:17:34,625
It's Zanth!

415
00:17:34,625 --> 00:17:37,416
Zane found us!

416
00:17:37,416 --> 00:17:39,833
Zane looks... different.

417
00:17:40,750 --> 00:17:41,750
Pixal!

418
00:17:42,833 --> 00:17:43,916
Where were you?

419
00:17:43,916 --> 00:17:44,875
How'd you find us?

420
00:17:44,875 --> 00:17:46,375
Zane's been looking for you!

421
00:17:46,375 --> 00:17:48,166
Yes, we found each other.

422
00:17:51,500 --> 00:17:52,750
[grunting]

423
00:17:52,750 --> 00:17:54,250
H'yah!

424
00:17:54,250 --> 00:17:56,750
Somebody had a glow up.

425
00:18:00,083 --> 00:18:01,250
We haven't met.

426
00:18:01,250 --> 00:18:02,583
I am Pixal.

427
00:18:02,583 --> 00:18:04,125
I don't care!

428
00:18:04,125 --> 00:18:05,166
You should.

429
00:18:05,166 --> 00:18:07,291
You are attacking my friend,

430
00:18:07,291 --> 00:18:09,750
and that is something
I will not tolerate.

431
00:18:09,750 --> 00:18:10,583
Ah!

432
00:18:12,875 --> 00:18:16,458
Dragonians, pull back!

433
00:18:16,458 --> 00:18:19,083
We can always find you, Ninja,

434
00:18:19,083 --> 00:18:20,708
and when we return,

435
00:18:20,708 --> 00:18:23,041
you will give us the blade

436
00:18:23,041 --> 00:18:25,125
or die defending it!

437
00:18:25,125 --> 00:18:26,708
The what?

438
00:18:26,708 --> 00:18:27,833
The blade!

439
00:18:27,833 --> 00:18:30,166
You will give us the blade!

440
00:18:30,166 --> 00:18:31,291
Parade?

441
00:18:31,291 --> 00:18:33,625
Why would we give you
a parade?

442
00:18:33,625 --> 00:18:35,000
That's not what I said!

443
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,750
We'll never throw you a parade.

444
00:18:36,750 --> 00:18:38,583
'Cause of how you're evil.

445
00:18:38,583 --> 00:18:40,125
[growling] Bah!

446
00:18:41,583 --> 00:18:44,041
He clearly said "blade"
not "parade".

447
00:18:44,041 --> 00:18:45,041
I know.

448
00:18:45,041 --> 00:18:47,166
Pixal!
Oh, you're back!

449
00:18:47,166 --> 00:18:49,958
And Zane, you're... huge?

450
00:18:49,958 --> 00:18:51,208
What happened?

451
00:18:51,208 --> 00:18:52,833
We will explain everything--

452
00:18:52,833 --> 00:18:54,333
--but first, you must know

453
00:18:54,333 --> 00:18:56,166
the Five are gathering
special blades

454
00:18:56,166 --> 00:18:58,500
for an unidentified
nefarious purpose.

455
00:18:58,500 --> 00:19:01,041
Yeah, blades like this.

456
00:19:01,041 --> 00:19:02,250
It looks different,

457
00:19:02,250 --> 00:19:03,541
but it sounds the same

458
00:19:03,541 --> 00:19:05,500
as the sword
from my fight with Zeatrix.

459
00:19:06,708 --> 00:19:09,333
It is made of
the same kind of rare metal

460
00:19:09,333 --> 00:19:10,541
that sword was.

461
00:19:11,375 --> 00:19:13,583
But why would the Five
want them?

462
00:19:16,291 --> 00:19:20,000
You let the Ninja
get the blade?

463
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,500
They already had it.

464
00:19:21,500 --> 00:19:22,333
I couldn't--

465
00:19:22,333 --> 00:19:23,833
Ah!

466
00:19:23,833 --> 00:19:24,958
Fail me again

467
00:19:24,958 --> 00:19:26,291
and the Forbidden Five

468
00:19:26,291 --> 00:19:27,916
will be the Forbidden Four!

469
00:19:29,458 --> 00:19:30,958
Kur,

470
00:19:30,958 --> 00:19:33,416
tell me you didn't also fail!

471
00:19:33,416 --> 00:19:35,375
I got the blade,

472
00:19:35,375 --> 00:19:37,875
but I found it like this.

473
00:19:39,958 --> 00:19:41,166
Hmm...

474
00:19:41,166 --> 00:19:42,875
We can fix it.

475
00:19:42,875 --> 00:19:45,750
All it will take
is a little wish magic.

476
00:19:45,750 --> 00:19:48,083
But all the Djinn are gone.

477
00:19:48,083 --> 00:19:50,166
No.

478
00:19:50,166 --> 00:19:53,333
Not all of them.

479
00:20:04,541 --> 00:20:06,083
You said they'd be here.

480
00:20:10,250 --> 00:20:11,416
No tricks?

481
00:20:11,416 --> 00:20:12,458
No lies?

482
00:20:12,458 --> 00:20:14,291
This is real,
my parents are there?

483
00:20:14,291 --> 00:20:16,125
No lies.

484
00:20:19,583 --> 00:20:20,666
Mom?

485
00:20:20,666 --> 00:20:21,666
Dad?

486
00:20:24,666 --> 00:20:25,666
No...

487
00:20:29,750 --> 00:20:31,666
[panting]

488
00:20:37,791 --> 00:20:40,041
[thunder rumbling]

489
00:20:41,250 --> 00:20:43,833
[panting]

490
00:20:44,833 --> 00:20:46,333
Mom! Dad!

491
00:20:46,333 --> 00:20:48,458
No!

492
00:20:48,458 --> 00:20:50,458
[crying]

493
00:20:52,375 --> 00:20:54,166
Why didn't you tell me?

494
00:20:54,166 --> 00:20:57,083
Would you have believed me
without seeing it for yourself?

495
00:20:57,083 --> 00:20:58,875
No.

496
00:20:58,875 --> 00:21:00,666
How did they die?

497
00:21:00,666 --> 00:21:02,791
That is unclear.

498
00:21:02,791 --> 00:21:04,000
Whatever happened,

499
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:07,000
it must've been
because of the Merge.

500
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:09,125
But I can fix it all.

501
00:21:09,125 --> 00:21:10,708
"Fix it"?

502
00:21:10,708 --> 00:21:11,916
They're dead!

503
00:21:11,916 --> 00:21:13,916
There's nothing to fix anymore.

504
00:21:13,916 --> 00:21:17,208
Not true.

505
00:21:17,208 --> 00:21:18,958
Reverse the Merge,

506
00:21:18,958 --> 00:21:22,000
and you can create
anything in its wake,

507
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:25,208
and I will reverse the Merge.

508
00:21:25,208 --> 00:21:28,458
That's why I, alone,
can save them.

509
00:21:28,458 --> 00:21:32,000
What exactly are you saying?

510
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:33,791
Your parents.

511
00:21:33,791 --> 00:21:35,208
My people.

512
00:21:35,208 --> 00:21:39,083
Help me undo the Merge,
and they will return,

513
00:21:39,083 --> 00:21:41,041
restored to life

514
00:21:41,041 --> 00:21:43,750
like nothing ever happened.

515
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:46,791
[♪♪♪]

